---
title: CI defensive guards
description: Repository RLS discipline and CI automation to prevent tenant-scope drift (Phase 5).
---

# CI defensive guards

Codifies **Postgres RLS session binding** rules for `@apps/api` repository layers and the CI guard that catches drift before merge.

Related: [`list-projection-guards.mdoc`](list-projection-guards.mdoc) (AP5 bookings two-step) · [`error-handling-standard.mdoc`](error-handling-standard.mdoc) (AP14).

## RLS policy contract (tenant-scoped tables)

Every tenant-owned table must ship:

```sql
ALTER TABLE <table> ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE <table> FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY <table>_tenant_isolation ON <table>
  USING (tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id', true)::uuid)
  WITH CHECK (tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id', true)::uuid);
```

App pool role (`app_tour`) uses `NOBYPASSRLS`; queries without `withTenantRls` return zero rows.

## Repository rules

| Pattern | When | Example |
|---------|------|---------|
| **`withTenantRls(tenantId, tx => …)`** | Tenant known at call site | `listPendingInvitesByTenant`, `createPendingInvite` |
| **Admin probe + RLS fetch** | PK-only lookup; tenant unknown at repo boundary | `listOutboxByAggregate` — admin `select: { tenantId }` then `withTenantRls` outbox read |
| **Tenant-scoped PK read** | Tenant known at call site | `getById(id, tenantId)` — `withTenantRls` only (no admin probe) |
| **Global / non-tenant tables** | Exempt from guard | `users`, `mobile_otp_challenges`, platform registry |

Implementation: [`apps/api/src/db/with-tenant-rls.ts`](../../apps/api/src/db/with-tenant-rls.ts).

## Identity — `operator_pending_invites` (Phase 5)

Table gained RLS in migration `20260707110000_operator_pending_invites_rls`.

| Repository method | Pattern |
|-------------------|---------|
| `createPendingInvite` | `withTenantRls(input.tenantId, tx => tx.operatorPendingInvite.create(...))` |
| `listPendingInvitesByTenant` | `withTenantRls(tenantId, tx => tx.findMany(...))` |
| `findPendingInvite(tenantId, inviteId)` | `withTenantRls` + `findFirst({ inviteId, tenantId })` |
| `findPendingInviteByToken(tenantId, token)` | `withTenantRls` + `findFirst({ inviteToken, tenantId })` |
| `revokePendingInvite(tenantId, inviteId)` | `withTenantRls` + `delete({ where: { inviteId } })` |
| `acceptPendingInvite(tenantId, token, userId)` | Scoped token lookup inside `withTenantRls` transaction |

Service callers pass `auth.tenantId` from [`invites.service.ts`](../../apps/api/src/identity/invites.service.ts) and [`users.service.ts`](../../apps/api/src/identity/users.service.ts).

## Guard — `guard:repository-rls`

**Script:** [`scripts/guards/guard-repository-rls.mjs`](../../scripts/guards/guard-repository-rls.mjs)

**Scope:** `apps/api/src/**/*.repository.ts` (excludes `in-memory-*.repository.ts`)

**Rule:** A repository method that calls `getPrisma().<tenantModel>` must contain `withTenantRls(` in the same method body, **or** use `getPrismaAdmin()` (admin probe allowlist), **or** appear in `LEGACY_ALLOWLIST`.

**Initial tenant models:** `operatorPendingInvite`, `operatorRegistration`, `tour`, `userTenant`, `outboxEvent`, `payment`, `paymentReceipt`, `exposureProfile`, `exposureIntent`, `integrationConnection`, `integrationDeliveryJob`.

**Run:**

```bash
pnpm run guard:repository-rls
```

Included in `phase-6:fast-track` after `guard:catch-error-leak`.

## Guard — `guard:bookings-getbyid-tenant-scope`

**Script:** [`scripts/guards/guard-bookings-getbyid-tenant-scope.mjs`](../../scripts/guards/guard-bookings-getbyid-tenant-scope.mjs)

**Scope:** `apps/api/src/bookings/prisma-bookings.repository.ts`

**Rules:**

1. `getById` signature includes `tenantId: string`.
2. `getById` body uses `withTenantRls` and does **not** call `getPrismaAdmin()`.
3. Any `getPrismaAdmin().operatorRegistration` probe in the file uses `select: { tenantId: true }` only (today: `listOutboxByAggregate`).

**Run:**

```bash
pnpm run guard:bookings-getbyid-tenant-scope
```

Included in `phase-6:fast-track` after `guard:repository-rls`.

## Guard — `guard:unbounded-list` (AP15 tightened)

**Script:** [`scripts/guards/guard-unbounded-list.mjs`](../../scripts/guards/guard-unbounded-list.mjs)

**Scope:** `apps/api/src/**/*.repository.ts` (excludes `in-memory-*.repository.ts`, `platform/`)

**Rule:** Tenant-scoped `findMany` must include **`take:`** or **`select:` with bounded `where.in`**. `select` alone (full tenant scan) **FAILs**.

**Run:** `pnpm run guard:unbounded-list`

## Guard — `guard:repository-n-plus-one` (AP15b)

**Script:** [`scripts/guards/guard-repository-n-plus-one.mjs`](../../scripts/guards/guard-repository-n-plus-one.mjs)

**Rule:** No `await` + Prisma delegate call inside `for` loops in repository files (batch exceptions allowlisted per file).

**Run:** `pnpm run guard:repository-n-plus-one`

## Audit — `audit:findmany-scan`

**Script:** [`scripts/audit-findmany-scan.mjs`](../../scripts/audit-findmany-scan.mjs)

**Rule:** FAIL when any repository `findMany` uses `select` without `take` (select-only unbounded).

Wired into `phase-6:fast-track` after `guard:repository-n-plus-one`.

