## Identity — directory avatar batching (Phase 5c)

Operator directory responses include signed avatar URLs. The service must **not** call MinIO setup per row.

| Layer | Pattern |
|-------|---------|
| [`operator-avatar-storage.ts`](../../apps/api/src/identity/operator-avatar-storage.ts) | `resolveOperatorAvatarUrlsForMemberships` — one env read + one MinIO client per batch |
| [`users.service.ts`](../../apps/api/src/identity/users.service.ts) | `directoryRowsFromPairs` maps `{ user, membership }[]` → `UsersDirectoryRow[]` with batched presign |

Read-path rules:

- **No** `ensureTenantBrandLogoBucket` on directory load (upload path still ensures bucket on `putOperatorAvatar`).
- **Early exit** when no row has a non-empty `storageKey` — all `avatarUrl: null` without touching MinIO.
- **`listUsersDirectory`**: SQL pagination via `countMembershipsDirectory` + `listMembershipsWithUsersDirectoryPage`, then one `directoryRowsFromPairs(pairs)` for avatar presign.
- **Bulk mutations** (`runBulkMutation`, `bulkRemoveWorkspaceUsers`): collect `{ user, membership }` success pairs, then one `directoryRowsFromPairs` at the end.

**Static checks:** `test/operator-avatar-batch.spec.ts` (AVT-BATCH-01/02) · `test/service-batch-patterns.spec.ts` (SVC-BATCH-03..05) · `test/identity-directory-pagination.spec.ts` (ID-DIR-01..04).

## Identity — directory SQL pagination (Phase 5c — repository)

Operator directory paginates in the repository — not load-all then filter/slice in `users.service`.

| Repository method | Pattern |
|-------------------|---------|
| `countMembershipsDirectory` | `withTenantRls` + `userTenant.count({ where: buildUserTenantDirectoryWhere(...) })` |
| `listMembershipsWithUsersDirectoryPage` | SQL `skip`/`take` or raw `ORDER BY displayName` for name sorts |
| `findUsersByIds(userIds)` | Global `users.findMany` with bounded `in` — bulk prefetch, role history actor lookup |
| `findMembershipsByUserIds(tenantId, userIds)` | `userTenant.findMany` with bounded `in` — bulk mutation prefetch |

Filters: [`users-directory-list-projection.ts`](../../apps/api/src/identity/users-directory-list-projection.ts) · in-memory sort parity: [`users-directory-query.ts`](../../apps/api/src/identity/users-directory-query.ts).

## Exposure — batch intent reads (Phase 5d)

| Repository method | Pattern |
|-------------------|---------|
| `findForContexts(contexts[])` | Single `withTenantRls` + `findMany({ OR: [...keys] })` keyed by profile/surface/audience/trigger/scopeHash |
| `listForConnectionScope` (control plane) | Hoist **once per connection** before event-type loop; pass `connectionIntents` into `resolveConnectionExposureIntentForRoute` |

## Identity — bulk mutation prefetch (Phase 5e)

| Pattern | Detail |
|---------|--------|
| `loadBulkUserMutationPrefetch` | `findMembershipsByUserIds` + `findUsersByIds` before bulk loop |
| `runBulkMutation` | Passes prefetch into per-user mutators — skips redundant membership/user lookups; batch avatar presign via `directoryRowsFromPairs(successPairs)` |
| `bulkRemoveWorkspaceUsers` | Same prefetch helper as role/status bulk paths |

## Identity — member booking summary (Phase 5e)

`getWorkspaceUserBookingSummary` must not call `listByTenant` then filter in memory.

| Pattern | Detail |
|---------|--------|
| Count queries | `countBookingsBySubmittedUser`, `countCancelledBookingsBySubmittedUser`, `countCompletedTripsBySubmittedUser` |
| Recent trips | `listRecentBySubmittedUser(tenantId, userId, MAX_MEMBER_BOOKINGS_RECENT_TRIPS)` |
| Service | `compileUserBookingSummaryFromCounts` in [`compile-user-booking-summary.ts`](../../apps/api/src/identity/compile-user-booking-summary.ts) |

**Static checks:** `test/bookings-member-summary-projection.spec.ts` (BK-MEM-01..03).

## Integrations — event policy sync (Phase 5e)

Policy upserts belong in infrastructure, not `*service.ts` loops:

| Module | Role |
|--------|------|
| `sync-integration-event-policies.ts` | `parseIntegrationEventPolicyPatches` + `syncIntegrationEventPoliciesInTransaction` |
| `patchIntegration` | Validates against provider `defaultEventPolicies`, delegates sync to infrastructure |

## Deferred (Phase 5b+)

- `guard-workspace-export-surface` — Denali `package.json` allowlist (Phase 6)

## Cross-tenant admin paths (Phase 5b)

Some operations intentionally span all tenant memberships for a global user (e.g. mobile change invalidates sessions everywhere). These **must** use `getPrismaAdmin()` — never `getPrisma().userTenant.*` without `withTenantRls`, because app pool RLS would silently update zero rows.

| Method | Pattern |
|--------|---------|
| `updateUserMobile` | `getPrisma()` transaction for global `users` row; then `getPrismaAdmin().userTenant.updateMany({ where: { userId } })` to bump `sessionVersion` on all memberships |

## Guard — `guard:service-n-plus-one`

**Script:** [`scripts/guards/guard-service-n-plus-one.mjs`](../../scripts/guards/guard-service-n-plus-one.mjs)

**Scope:** `apps/api/src/**/*service.ts`

**Rule:** A service method must not contain `await` + repository/Prisma read/write inside `for`/`for-of`/`for-in`/`while` loops or `array.map(async …)` / `Promise.all(…map(async))` unless the method is on `LEGACY_ALLOWLIST` (known baseline violations) or `ADMIN_ALLOWLIST` (migration/dev-only paths).

**Suspicious patterns in loop bodies:** `.find*`, `.list*`, `.get*`, `.create*`, `.update*`, `.upsert*`, `.remove*`, `getPrisma`, `withTenantRls`, `Repository(`.

**Run:**

```bash
pnpm run guard:service-n-plus-one
```

Included in `phase-6:fast-track` after `guard:repository-rls`.

## Exposure control plane — batch reads (Phase 5f)

The control plane previously issued per-connection and per-event-type repository calls inside loops. Batch contracts:

| Repository | Batch method | Replaces |
|------------|--------------|----------|
| `ExposureIntentRepository` | `listForConnectionScopes({ tenantId, connectionIds })` | N× `listForConnectionScope` in `Promise.all(…map(async))` |
| `ExposureIntentRepository` | `findForContexts(contexts)` (existing) | Per-event `findForContext` legacy fallback |
| `ExposureProfileRepository` | `ensureSeededProfiles({ tenantId, seeds })` | Per-context `ensureSeededProfile` in event loop |

**Orchestration:** `getWorkspaceExposureControlPlane` prefetches intents + legacy lookups + profiles in ≤3 queries, then builds contexts synchronously via `buildConnectionContextsFromPrefetch` (no `await` in loops).

**Static checks:** `test/exposure-batch-reads.spec.ts` (EXP-BATCH-01..04).

## CI wiring (defensive bundle)

The AP14/AP15 guards below are bundled in **`phase-6:defensive-guards`** ([`scripts/phase-6-defensive-guards.sh`](../../scripts/phase-6-defensive-guards.sh)) — single source of truth for local and CI static enforcement.

| Path | Command / workflow | When |
|------|-------------------|------|
| **Local iteration** | `pnpm run phase-6:defensive-guards` | After API/repo changes (~2–5 min, no Postgres) |
| **Local full loop** | `pnpm run phase-6:fast-track` | `pre-commit:fast` + defensive bundle |
| **GHA PR (static)** | Job `defensive-guards` in [`.github/workflows/phase-6-gate.yml`](../../.github/workflows/phase-6-gate.yml) | Every PR + push to `main` (parallel, no Postgres) |
| **GHA PR (registry)** | `guard:workspace-registry-fresh` in [`.github/workflows/phase-3-gate.yml`](../../.github/workflows/phase-3-gate.yml) | Every PR before `phase-3:gate` |
| **GHA behavioral** | Job `fast-closure` in `phase-6-gate.yml` | Build + test + Postgres (unchanged) |

**Bundle contents:** `guard:import-boundary`, denali/urban plugin surfaces, `guard:workspace-plugin-surface` (via guest-plugin-conformance), workspace export surface, `guard:api-workspace-isolation`, field-policy, unbounded-list, repository-n-plus-one, `audit:findmany-scan`, list-projection-openapi, catch-error-leak (all `apps/api/src/**`), repository-rls, bookings-getbyid-tenant-scope, service-n-plus-one, **identity directory static specs** (`operator-avatar-batch`, `service-batch-patterns`, `identity-directory-pagination`, `bookings-member-summary-projection`), WRS/PCMS, guest-plugin-conformance (includes `guard:workspace-peer-import`), `guard:workspace-onboard-contract`, `guard:workspace-certification`, `guard:admin-inline-color`, `guard:todo-debt-budget`, `phase-6:guard`.

**Workspace onboarding:** `pnpm run workspace:onboard -- <id> [--guest]` runs install, codegen, domain checks, build, test, and conformance guards ([`scripts/workspace-onboard.mjs`](../../scripts/workspace-onboard.mjs)).

**Import boundary:** `IMPORT_BOUNDARY_SCAN_ROOTS` includes all of `packages/workspaces/`; relative `types/legacy/` imports within a workspace package are allowed (Denali product types, not monorepo `legacy/`).

**Not in bundle (separate workflows):** `control:ci` (CTL-CORE visual packs), `phase-10-guard` (path-filtered workspace host invariants).

**Also in `ci:integrity`:** `guard:workspace-registry-fresh` (early) + full `phase-6:defensive-guards` (after evolution gate).

